nd during the course of the investigation, it was found that the rooms were not well ventilated after being painted, infants were placed in the cafeteria with children older than 18 months and no amendment was requested to licensing, the director also did not notify the operation that their playground had been finished for inspection and review, and the director chose to end a safety plan without discussing it with Licensing during the course of the investigation.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026547453","violation_type_title":"Director Responsibilities - Operate in Compliance (26 TAC §746.1003(1))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-94748-i20230829-v2","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-1201-1","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-94748-i20230829","date":"2023-08-29","original_code":"746.1201(1)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2023-11-07","finding":"Responsibilities of Employees and Caregivers -Demonstrate Competency, Good Judgment, Self-control: Based on the information obtained during the course of the investigation, the operation used poor judgment when they allowed children and staff to be placed in classrooms after being painted. As a result, staff became ill and it is believed that some of the infants became ill while being in care as well. After there had been complaints of the smell the infant children were moved for one day and then placed back into their classrooms.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026547450","violation_type_title":"Responsibilities of Employees and Caregivers -Demonstrate Competency, Good Judgment, Self-control (26 TAC §746.1201(1))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"}]},{"id":"tx-hhsc-94748-i20230719","date":"2023-07-19","inspection_type":"Inspection","result":"No deficiencies cited","passed":true,"violation_count":0,"open_count":0,"evidence_class":"VERIFIED","provenance":{"source_id":"tx_hhsc_activities","source_record_id":"905742213"