ng Immunizations, Administering Medication, Food Allergies, Building and Premises Safety, Hazardous Materials including Blood Borne Pathogens, and Emergency Preparedness Trainings    One out of four staff was missing Communicable Diseases including Immunizations, Administering Medication, and Hazardous Materials including Blood Borne Pathogens. This is a re-cite.","topic":"staffing","source_record_id":"1026705314","violation_type_title":"Training Requirements for Employees and Caregivers -  24 Annual Training (26 TAC §746.1301(5)(A))","topic_label":"Staff qualifications & clearances"}]},{"id":"tx-hhsc-94748-i20220713","date":"2022-07-13","inspection_type":"Inspection","result":"Deficiencies cited","passed":false,"violation_count":4,"open_count":0,"evidence_class":"VERIFIED","provenance":{"source_id":"tx_hhsc_activities","source_record_id":"905742210","url":"https://data.texas.gov/resource/m5q4-3y3d.json?activity_id=905742210","retrieved_at":"2026-11-05T21:27:29.718Z","effective_date":"2022-07-13","evidence_class":"VERIFIED"},"occurrences":[{"id":"tx-hhsc-94748-i20220713-v1","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-5205-1","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-94748-i20220713","date":"2022-07-13","original_code":"746.5205(1)","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2022-08-05","finding":"Fire Drill Monthly - Exit in 3 Minutes: The operation did not have documentation of fire drills, severe weather, or lock down drills. There was also no monthly  documentation for smoke alarms, fire extinguishers, or carbon monoxide detectors.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026475419","violation_type_title":"Fire Drill Monthly - Exit in 3 Minutes (26 TAC §746.5205(1))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-94748-i20220713-v2","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-3819","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-94748-i20220713","date":"2022-07-13","original_code":"746.3819","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2022-08-05","finding":"Food Allergy Emergency Plan Signed by Parents and Health Care Professional: One child who has a documented food allergy did not have a food allergy plan on file.","topic":"fire","source_record_id":"1026274885","violation_type_title":"Food Allergy Emergency Plan Signed by Parents and Health Care Professional (26 TAC §746.3819)","topic_label":"Fire safety & emergency drills"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-94748-i20220713-v3","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-1301-5-a","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-94748-i20220713","date":"2022-07-13","original_code":"746.1301(5)(A)","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2022-08-05","finding":"Training Requirements for Employees and Caregivers -  24 Annual Training: One out of four staff did not have the required 30 hours of annual training for 2020-2021. The following trainings were missing: child maltreatment, sids, shaken baby, and early brain development, transportation, and all trainings in standard 746.1311(e).    One out of four staff did not have the required 24 hours of annual training for 2021-2022. They were missing 2 1/2 hours of annual training. The following trainings were missing: child maltreatment, sids, shaken baby, and early brain development, and all trainings in section 746.1309 (e) with the exception of medication which was found in the file.    One out of four staff did not have the required 24 hours of training and were still missing 11 1/2 hours of training for 2020-2021. The staff member was missing trainings in section 746.1309 (e).     One out of four staff was missing trainings from standard 746.1309 (e).","topic":"staffing","source_record_id":"1026315187","violation_type_title":"Training Requirements for Employees and Caregivers -  24 Annual Training (26 TAC §746.1301(5)(A))","topic_label":"Staff qualifications & clearances"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-94748-i20220713-v4","